    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0822" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/823: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-02-17T20:00:00+09:00">February 17,
                            1939—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 18—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. Department’s 17, January 19, 9 p.m., Canton Maritime Customs. The procedure
                    envisaged in Department’s paragraph numbered 1 was followed in an interview with
                    the Minister for Foreign Affairs today. The Minister replied that he took note
                    of my statement but made no further comment.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d815-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d815-f1" n="56" xml:id="d815-f1-content">
                <p>See Ambassador Grew’s memorandum of February 17, <ref
